description: |
    Test metadata, e.g. plans stored in a remote repository, are cloned and
    processed by tmt on the runner. URLs from such metadata were passed
    to ``git clone`` and to the archive download & extraction without any
    validation, depending entirely on the default configuration of the
    deployment to stay safe:

    * git remote helper URLs, most notably ``ext::<command>``, execute
      an arbitrary command when cloned. They are refused by git's default
      ``protocol.ext.allow = never``, however tmt itself did not validate
      the transport at all. URLs provided by the ``url`` keys of the
      ``discover`` and ``prepare`` steps, by ``import`` plan references
      and by beakerlib libraries are now validated by tmt: only ``http``,
      ``https``, ``git`` and ``ssh`` (including aliases such as
      ``git+ssh``) URLs, scp-like addresses and local paths are allowed,
      and URLs resembling command line options are rejected as well.
    * archives downloaded for ``discover`` with
      ``url-content-type: archive`` are now extracted with Python's
      ``data`` filter, refusing members outside of the extraction
      directory (previously a crafted archive could write files anywhere
      the tmt process could write, e.g. as root inside the Testing Farm
      worker container). The download itself now accepts only ``http``
      and ``https`` URLs.
